# Shopping Mode (Epic E5)

> Branch: `jingduo-develop` ｜ Author: Jingduo Zhang (jzha0609)
> Scope: KitchMemo shopping cart feature (Epic E5 — Shopping Assistant & Smart Cart)

Brings household inventory into the shopping journey: review what's at home, build a cart, warn about possible duplicate purchases, review at checkout, and turn completed purchases into inventory records.

---

## Feature overview (against the backlog)

| User Story | Feature | Status |
|---|---|---|
| US5.1 | Review household stock before shopping (read-only peek) | ✅ |
| US5.2 | Build a cart: add (manual / photo), edit quantity, delete | ✅ |
| US5.3 | Duplicate-purchase warning (expandable, per-batch quantity/storage/expiry) | ✅ |
| US5.4 | Checkout review: list all items, highlight duplicate warnings | ✅ |
| US5.5 | Turn purchases into inventory drafts, edit-and-confirm, leave prompt | ✅ |
| — | Photo recognition into the cart (reuses the team model, Plan A) | ✅ |

**Not done / notes**: the recognition model itself is built by the team (recognises 8 fruit/veg only); units are not localised (the stored string is shown as-is); full inventory browsing (US5.1.2) stays on the Fridge tab — Shopping Mode only provides a read-only peek.

